# Spork 19 turned off, then a KILL: the load reverts it to the last store, on (O2b D34), and a
# lock conflicts with a fork block again. The tip's INVALIDATE first keeps S2's header line from
# tying with the load (G-T1: the input's own invalidation does not count).
extend main 2
invalidate main@-0
spork off
restart kill
cl main@-0
fork 1 1
